<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Habiby LLC
  SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

  Entitlements for the Developer ID build: the DMG on GitHub Releases, the
  channel that updates itself (release-engineering §5, §6). The Mac App Store
  build signs with Entitlements.plist.

  The same iCloud Documents container as the store build, so both channels
  offer iCloud Drive › Proscenium with no folder panel (storage §12). Apple's
  capability table lists "iCloud: iCloud documents" for Developer ID, and it
  needs a Developer ID provisioning profile, which the release workflow embeds
  as Contents/embedded.provisionprofile. It also adds the application and team
  identifiers, read from that profile, because codesign does not expand
  Xcode's $(TeamIdentifierPrefix).

    icloud-container-identifiers   the app's own container,
    ubiquity-container-identifiers shown in Finder as
    icloud-services                iCloud Drive › Proscenium
    icloud-container-environment   Production: the only environment a
                                   Developer ID build may use

  NOT sandboxed, and that is the difference from the store build.
  tauri-plugin-updater replaces the app bundle in /Applications, which the App
  Sandbox forbids, so a sandboxed download could fetch an update and never
  install it (tauri-apps/tauri#8258, open since 2023). Hardened runtime and
  notarization still apply; the store build keeps the sandbox, and there the
  store does the updating.

  An ad-hoc build (a local install, the CI self-test) signs with no
  entitlements at all: an app that claims iCloud without a profile is killed
  at launch.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
  <array>
    <string>iCloud.org.habiby.proscenium</string>
  </array>

  <key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-container-identifiers</key>
  <array>
    <string>iCloud.org.habiby.proscenium</string>
  </array>

  <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
  <array>
    <string>CloudDocuments</string>
  </array>

  <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-environment</key>
  <string>Production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
